42
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:24.384
Your turn. Say: privacy policy.

43
00:02:27.084 --> 00:02:28.608
privacy policy.

44
00:02:29.617 --> 00:02:31.709
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:32.009 --> 00:02:35.506
I keep seeing targeted ads for things I only talked about!

46
00:02:36.817 --> 00:02:40.572
Tracking is everywhere. Did you read the app's privacy policy?

47
00:02:41.883 --> 00:02:45.873
No. I just clicked accept. I admit not reading it.

48
00:02:47.183 --> 00:02:51.821
Most people do the same. Companies are accused of collecting data without real consent.

49
00:02:53.117 --> 00:02:56.567
My friend refused to use facial recognition at her bank.

50
00:02:57.883 --> 00:03:01.662
Wise. I'd recommend turning on encryption and checking your settings.

51
00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:06.703
Grammar focus: Verb patterns with reporting verbs.

52
00:03:07.003 --> 00:03:09.583
Many reporting verbs have their own patterns.

53
00:03:09.883 --> 00:03:12.857
Accuse someone of doing, recommend doing, refuse to do.

54
00:03:13.157 --> 00:03:18.570
For example: They accused the company of selling data, and experts recommend using encryption.

55
00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:24.318
Some reporting verbs need a preposition: accuse of, blame for, apologise for, insist on.

56
00:03:25.317 --> 00:03:27.876
Now read and listen. Who Owns Your Data?.

57
00:03:28.176 --> 00:03:31.789
Every time we go online, our actions create valuable data.

58
00:03:33.083 --> 00:03:37.138
Companies use tracking to show us targeted ads and predict our choices.

59
00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:42.249
Critics accuse some tech firms of collecting data without clear consent.

60
00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:47.419
Governments have introduced data protection laws to give people more control.

61
00:03:48.717 --> 00:03:53.642
Experts recommend reading the privacy policy and using encryption whenever possible.

62
00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:57.312
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:57.612 --> 00:03:59.681
Permission for something to happen is blank.

64
00:03:59.981 --> 00:04:03.495
A, consent. B, tracking. C, encryption.

65
00:04:07.483 --> 00:04:09.483
The answer is A: consent.

66
00:04:10.983 --> 00:04:12.507
They accused him blank the money.

67
00:04:12.807 --> 00:04:16.263
A, to steal. B, of stealing. C, for steal.

68
00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:22.203
The answer is B: of stealing.

69
00:04:23.717 --> 00:04:26.610
I recommend blank two-step verification.

70
00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:30.018
A, to use. B, using. C, use.

71
00:04:34.017 --> 00:04:35.540
The answer is B: using.

72
00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:40.060
Changing information into a secret code is blank.

73
00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:44.373
A, facial recognition. B, encryption. C, cyber attack.

74
00:04:48.383 --> 00:04:50.093
The answer is B: encryption.

75
00:04:51.583 --> 00:04:55.963
According to the text, why have governments introduced data protection laws?

76
00:04:56.263 --> 00:05:01.286
A, to sell data. B, to give people more control. C, to stop the internet.

77
00:05:05.283 --> 00:05:08.467
The answer is B: to give people more control.

78
00:05:09.983 --> 00:05:14.391
Now it's your turn to speak. Are you worried about your privacy online? Why?

79
00:05:19.691 --> 00:05:27.568
Yes. Many apps are accused of tracking us, so I recommend checking privacy settings and refusing unnecessary permissions.

80
00:05:27.868 --> 00:05:29.380
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:30.383 --> 00:05:35.067
Great work today! You learned eight new words and verb patterns with reporting verbs.

82
00:05:35.367 --> 00:05:39.726
Today's value is online safety. Keep your password secret and be kind online.

83
00:05:40.026 --> 00:05:42.830
See you in Unit twenty-eight. Goodbye!

84
00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:45.689
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

